<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Version>1.2.0</Version>
    <PackageId>TokenGuard.Core</PackageId>
    <Title>TokenGuard.Core</Title>
    <Authors>Svetlozar Stoykov</Authors>
    <Company>Svetlozar Stoykov</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Svetlozar Stoykov</Copyright>
    <Description>Token budget management for .NET 10 LLM agent loops. Tracks conversation growth, masks stale tool output, summarizes older history when needed, and keeps requests within a configured limit. Targets net10.0 only.</Description>
    <PackageTags>tokenguard;llm;ai;agents;context-management;token-budget;prompt-management;openai;anthropic;dotnet</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Tool-result masking moves its boundary in steps, so a prepared request is the previous one plus the new messages between two steps and a provider prompt cache can reuse it. Adds the provider's finish reason and token counts to summarizer diagnostics, and a package icon. Fixes the tool name on a masked result, diagnostics for a compaction strategy that throws, and repeated summarizer requests after a failure.

Behavior changes, with no signature changes: the default token budget is 40,000 instead of 25,000, so compaction starts at 32,000 tokens; prepared views mask further back at a step and differ from those of 1.1.0; the default placeholder of a masked result has a new, longer text; a call that starts while another call on the same context is still running throws InvalidOperationException; a recording call discards an exception thrown by a logger or meter listener; a failed summarizer call is not repeated while the history and the available tokens stay the same.

Known limits: summarization works with the built-in providers only, and a custom summarizer, compaction strategy, or token counter cannot be registered through the builder; one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas and undercount pretty-printed JSON by 17% to 30% until the first provider report; one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.

Full details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="TokenGuard.Tests" />
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="TokenGuard.IntegrationTests" />
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="TokenGuard.Extensions.OpenAI" />
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="TokenGuard.Extensions.Anthropic" />
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Codexplorer" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
